(600072, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: center; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">\nTrade Secrets</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: justify; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">For hundreds of years or more, among the unquestioned business practices of the West are companies\' rights and prerogative to keep trade secrets. As with any widespread assumption, there are at least edge and corner cases where such practices fall squarely out of justification, and into criminal activity.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: justify; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">Upon close inspection, the character of a practice, custom, or behavior can be predicted based on its motives. Are they honorable, necessary, and prudent? Or are they deceptive, manipulative, and self-serving? Trade secrets and secrets of any kind are justifiable only in the presence of substantial, measurable danger to the health and safety of a person or business. Otherwise, secrets form deception by way of omission. Herein lies the great folly of public acceptance of secrets as normal, necessary practice in business and government. That is, just because something has been the common way, doesn\'t mean it is the right way, or is it justified.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: justify; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">In fairness, examining trade secrets from both perspectives (pro and con), helps to establish their legitimacy. For example, it is a trade secret among manufacturers of disposable razors that the metal used in their blades is very precisely and scientifically softened with an alloy composition so as to ensure that they will be quickly disposed of. What if I told you that modern engineering could easily make a disposable razor for cheap that lasted virtually forever?</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: justify; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">We find that every instance of corporate trade secrets follows suit to this example, with a departure into the universe of Intellectual Property being the epitome of rhetoric in favor of trade secrets. \"How can our inventors be paid if their work is stolen?\" This concern has little if any substance or merit nowadays in that 1) almost every invention is derivative of another, 2) concerning the digitization of information, enforcement of patents and copyright has become impossible, and 3) the expectation of ownership of an idea and payment for its use is another unquestioned assumption, like that trade secrets are automatically great. The idea that an invention can or should belong to the inventor is a REACTION to the condition of capitalism that demands everyone work at figurative gunpoint. The underlying reality is that reconciliation of debt from someone taking credit for an idea or benefitting from its implementation, cannot be legislated. At the end of the day, this too is an honor system and our best hope is to encourage people to, when able, contribute to and compensate those from whose work they benefit.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: justify; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">Payment for services is always optional, especially when those services address vital necessities. A final incorrect, widespread assumption is that payment MUST be rendered for things like food, shelter, clothing, and taxes. Providing for all basic human needs is easily within the sphere of possibility when resources are not stolen, squandered, or secretly traded between conspiratorial, parasitic corporations and government entities.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; text-align: center; margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;font-size: 20px;\">end<br>\n</div>', '2022-07-18 12:57:50', 145, 76, 'whitehot robot', 'Trade Secrets', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600073, '<font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"CoinbaseSans, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, Fira Sans, Droid Sans, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif\" style=\"text-align: start;\">0xF41c3ed1bd1C7cb698D6a7155521596C24857Ba3 (POLYGON)&nbsp;</font><br style=\"text-align: start;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"CoinbaseSans, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, Fira Sans, Droid Sans, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif\" style=\"text-align: start;\">0x7Ae596D4d98e27F3f8C6da152017a9712C802F99 (ERC20)</font><br>', '2022-07-22 17:40:25', 145, 15, 'whitehot robot', 'polygon matic coinbase payway.dweet', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600074, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\">\n<center>domination and respect</center><br>\nA recurring theme in many self-proclaimed \"evil\" story lines, is the subversion of choices of another. Intuitively, most people understand that the right, proper thing is to maximize the liberty of others. In practice this resembles allowing them to make their own decisions in appearance, spirit, and reality.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\">But unfortunately, in authoritarian atmospheres one is expected to follow the rules set by a superior authority. Questioning the relevancy of the rules or the authority\'s qualifications is usually punished, as is defying the rules. Systems emerge for the indoctrination of \"managers\", new authority figures to make decisions for the \"less-qualified\", whereby the will of said managers is superimposed over that of their \"inferiors\".</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\">This practice of actively disabling the power and autonomy of individuals in lieu of a centralized code of conduct, when relied upon as a standard accepted means of maintaining social order, legitimizes subversion of free will in general by way of the leadership examples set by the authority. That is, it becomes acceptable and even expected that social and business dealings <b>should</b> involve selfish motives which extend unto achieving personal goals by any means necessary, as long as said means are within the behavior code. Obviously there can be no <b>COMPLETE </b>code of behavior, any more than there could be an atlas of clouds, so, ill-informed and guided solely by fear of punishment, every strong person becomes a predator, and everyone else a victim.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\">Herein lies the basis for terror and dysfunction of sexuality among youth and adults. When every adult is expected or permitted to make decisions for others, no impropriety is acknowledged when consent for sex is subverted, provided statutory stipulations are satisfied, but impropriety it still may be!</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\">To make someone\'s mind up for them is always improper unless the matter is one of group safety or self defense. In sexual matters especially, objective, un-coerced consent is the only valid consent. But <b><i><span style=\"font-size: 1.5em;\">those in the habit of choosing for others will view any opportunity for sex involving potentially vulnerable people as fundamentally improper</span></i></b>. Such is only the case when respect for the autonomy, knowledge, and valid, legitimate consent of the vulnerable, is violated by unscrupulous, selfish subversion of will.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; font-size: 20px\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2022-07-24 19:19:30', 145, 72, 'whitehot robot', 'domination and respect', '#psychology #morality #ethics', 0, 0, ''),
(600075, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; line-height: 1em;  font-size: 20px; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify;\">Dear ma\'am,</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; line-height: 1em;  font-size: 20px; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify;\">I\'m writing to say your last reply must have been lost in the mail, for I never received it. Search as I did, your words and certain invitation to festivities fell on the eyes of a thief, and not my own as you surely intended.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; line-height: 1em;  font-size: 20px; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify;\">I\'m afraid this problem has afflicted my address for as long as I\'ve lived here, and the only remedy is the old-fashioned, in-person introduction.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; line-height: 1em;  font-size: 20px; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify;\">In conclusion, please accept my warm regards and apology for not responding to your inquiries, as they never arrived.<br>\n</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; line-height: 1em;  font-size: 20px; color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify;\">Best</div>', '2022-07-24 22:18:01', 145, 70, 'whitehot robot', 'a thoughtful reply', '', 0, 0, ''),
