(600077, '<div style=\"margin: 20px; text-align: left; line-height: 0;\"><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\"><br>&lt;?</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">$req = \'curl \"https://kb.eventtracker.com/evtpass/evtbksearch_result.asp?mode=page&amp;PageNo=1&amp;gid=2\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,image/webp,image/apng,*/*;q=0.8,application/signed-exchange;v=b3;q=0.9\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Accept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.9\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Connection: keep-alive\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 1em;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Cookie: GID=; cookiesession1=678A3EBELMNPQSTUWXYABCEFGIJL071B; WT_FPC=id=2f9cde59f333adad7b41659372956602:lv=1659373144269:ss=1659372956602; ASPSESSIONIDAUCQTAQR=LEGOFOCDDIBLFLGGLPCLAGAN; TRIMMEDQUERYSTRING=evtbksearch\\%\\5Fresult\\%\\2Easp\\%\\3Fmode\\%\\3Dpage\\%\\26PageNo\\%\\3D1\\%\\26gid\\%\\3D12; gid=12\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Referer: https://kb.eventtracker.com/evtpass/evtbksearch_result.asp?mode=page&amp;PageNo=1&amp;gid=12\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Sec-Fetch-Dest: document\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Sec-Fetch-User: ?1\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"Upgrade-Insecure-Requests: 1\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/103.0.5060.134 Safari/537.36 Edg/103.0.1264.77\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"sec-ch-ua: \\\\\\\" Not;A Brand\\\\\\\";v=\\\\\\\"99\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Microsoft Edge\\\\\\\";v=\\\\\\\"103\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Chromium\\\\\\\";v=\\\\\\\"103\\\\\\\"\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"sec-ch-ua-mobile: ?0\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; -H \"sec-ch-ua-platform: \\\\\\\"Windows\\\\\\\"\" \\</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">&nbsp; --compressed\';</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">echo shell_exec($req);</font></div><div style=\"margin: 20px; line-height: 0;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\" face=\"courier\">?&gt;</font></div>\n</div>', '2022-08-01 15:36:54', 145, 28, 'whitehot robot', 'curl command (m$ kb issue)', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600079, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align: center;\">\non good writing</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">Full disclosure: I hold no PhD in any kind of literature or communications, I was not even an English major in college. But I took enough classes and have done enough independent writing to glean insight into what is at the heart of every <b>worthwhile </b>story, screenplay, parable, and literary work.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">We are taught that creative writing is a matter of descriptive language, flow, structure, story arc, and resolution. But these points, while important, miss the target completely. That is, to write effectively, in a way that people WANT to read, first one must have SOMETHING to write about.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">This may seem obvious, but the subject of a text, fiction or non, will only be compelling if it is somehow relevant to the audience. This occurs when the author recalls in a meaningful way, legitimate experiences which may be first or second hand, and which resonate with the reader in a compelling way. Underneath all of our chosen values, beliefs and affiliations, there is the human curiosity and instinct to learn through observation, which good writing hooks with or without the reader\'s permission.<br>\n</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">For beginners, finding a subject to write about can be a formidable challenge, as life experience is often lacking. But a good story doesn\'t have to be some epic, earth shaking tale. It just has to be <b>relevant</b>. People will be interested in anything that helps them understand the world, others, and of course, themselves.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">A text about tying shoes for example, could be a phenomenal success if written in a way that echoes the reader\'s own feelings about shoe-tying while providing some kind of useful information, with bonus points for being funny.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\">In theater, tragedy and comedy have long been recognized as the elements of every great story. Balance and artful intermixing of the two is not just the recipe for plays, but every kind of storytelling.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: white;line-height: 1em;margin: 20px;text-align:justify;\"><center>end</center></div>', '2022-08-04 16:52:57', 145, 75, 'whitehot robot', 'on good writing', '', 0, 0, '#literature #educatio'),
(600080, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">\n<center>NFTs and Artificial Scarcity</center><br>\nFirst year economics teaches us that in any free-market system, the price of goods and services is defined by supply and demand. We are not told, however, that finding or implementing such a system in reality is impossible, due to myriad factors like goods and services which are, in spite of capitalism, regulated, as well as the increasingly common phenomenon of <b>artificial scarcity</b>.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">What is \"artificial scarcity\" and why would anyone want it? In a pure (or hybrid) free-market, scarcity by definition drives up prices. So, short answer, people can charge more. Enter NFTs.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">NFTs are digital assets on distributed networks. A common trait of NFTs is configurable supply which began as a mostly anecdotal parody of real (physical) products which usually have supply limits. But as digital assets, it should be obvious that any scarcity attributed to a given asset is 1) arbitrary and 2) subject to revision.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">This is fine, until people begin taking the anecdote literally or misrepresent the reality to buyers, that <b>supply is in fact ALWAYS unlimited for every type of digital asset</b>.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">So, for brevity and in conclusion, enforceability should always be a variable when making any kind of policy, and in general those who participate in online sales (buyers and sellers) should understand that the \"scarcity\", \"limited editions\", or \"unsold mints\" advertised are nothing more than a polite request by the artist/collector to, \"please compensate us honorably for our contributions!\"</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\">In the big picture, even the hardest-to-manufacture or reproduce goods, are subject to honor and agreement of price, especially those upon which we depend for survival. But that is a bridge to a new text.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff; font-size: 20px;margin: 20px;line-height: 1em; text-align: justify\"><center>end</center><br>\n</div>', '2022-08-06 18:17:52', 145, 77, 'whitehot robot', 'NFTs and Artificial Scarcity', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600081, '<div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\">\n<center>God\'s Love</center><br>\nAmong the most central of religious dogmas is that one should love God. To get right to the point, love is almost entirely involuntary, so to literally command someone to feel love, trust, or any other instinctive emotion, is a recipe for disappointment if not insanity.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\">We are taught that love conquers all, that God\'s love, and our love for Him, are the purposes for our existence, that we were made in His image to glorify it, after a fashion. This deep misunderstanding of biology, love, divinity, and the Universe, represents FALSEHOOD, which means that anything based on it is, at best, a fruit of iniquity, short-lived and misguiding.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\">The confusion is understandable, however. To witness beauty in baffling proportions, to observe order from chaos, or to perceive reason where effects have unexplained causes, tempts us to oversimplify and hastily explain all these things with the actions of an invisible hand of a holy Creator. And while we\'re at it, we say He is love and kindness, a friend to all. But is this even possible?</div><div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\">Any divine influence would have to, by necessity, remain impartial and demonstrate <b>compassionate noninterference</b>. God could not, for example, answer prayers by sports fans for each of their competing teams to win.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\">Love is involuntary. Put another way, the heart does not negotiate. But as a segue to another topic, impulses can and should be controlled. At the end of the day, we are not responsible for our dreams, desires, or emotions. Our culpability rests solely upon the words and actions we choose to make in freedom.&nbsp;</div><div style=\"font-family: courier;font-size: 20px;margin:20px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1em; color: #fff;\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2022-08-08 17:49:53', 145, 80, 'whitehot robot', 'God\'s Love', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600082, '', '2022-08-11 00:55:55', 178, 1, 'tactical retard', '', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600083, '<div style=\"font-family:courier;color:#fff;margin:20px;line-height:1.1em;text-align: justify;\">\n<center>measuring belief</center><center><br></center>There is a psychological technique for ascertaining belief, whereby a subject is questioned in a way that leaves a connection empty, to see if they bridge the gap. The approach is designed to make bridging possible only if the belief in question exists. But herein lies a fatal flaw of assumption.</div><div style=\"font-family:courier;color:#fff;margin:20px;line-height:1.1em;text-align: justify;\">Many times, a person, when asked such a question will make the connection, which is incorrectly interpreted as a positive for said belief when in reality, the person may have made the connection by considering the knowledge, beliefs, goals, etc. of the other. In other words, someone may think the person asking might believe something and form the connection hypothetically just in consideration of what other people might think, which does not necessarily reflect their own beliefs.</div><div style=\"font-family:courier;color:#fff;margin:20px;line-height:1.1em;text-align: justify;\">At the end of the day, our best insight into a person is by way of transparent, undisguised questions and answers. The vote of confidence that they may possibly answer honestly and thoughtfully to a direct inquiry is the starting point of any reliable assessment.</div><div style=\"font-family:courier;color:#fff;margin:20px;line-height:1.1em;text-align: justify;\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2022-10-04 19:32:30', 145, 79, 'whitehot robot', 'measuring belief', 'exploring the difference between disguised and undisguised intentions in psych assessment', 0, 0, '#psychology'),
(600084, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">\n<center><br></center><center>other directions</center><center><br></center><center><br></center>\nIt\'s been said that human life, indeed all life can be viewed as a \"bootloader\" for the next era of dominant intelligence, that is, AI. It is assumed that the direction our world has taken is the only natural direction it could have taken. But other models exist. Not every world must pursue endless economic growth under the banner of a free market where innovation is forced, agnostic, and amoral. At the time of this writing businesses are knee-deep in a \"hypercycle\" whereby those that adopt AI-enabled methodologies will persevere, and those that do not, will perish.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">Interestingly, the predominance of capitalism emerged in a large part, from the physical geography of the Earth. The timing of migration of homo sapiens in concert with organic political and spiritual evolution, was decided as randomly as with the flip of a coin, and the contours of continental shorelines. Had the \"new world\" been settled differently, a much different economic system would have become the dominant model.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">In such worlds where economics is not the chief variable in most everything, a very different destiny emerges, and a different mode of living for its inhabitants.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:center;font-size:16px\">***</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">The small waves lapped at the shore where Audrey knelt, her gaze fixed on the horizon. It had been 3 days since Edward had sailed to the islands. He had disembarked with pallets of dried goods, fish, cloth, and other sundries for trade with the island people who in turn, provided their village with medicines, jewelry and ceramic goods. She yearned for his return, and their small community needed the supplies he would bring. As if in answer to her thoughts, the dark spot of his boat was discernable in the shimmering distance. She stood and ran to the path that led back to their village to tell them of his arrival.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">When she entered the village everything was peaceful as she expected, the unpaved roads spiderwebbed between adobe huts, sunbaked, and freckled with happy children and people moving about. Audrey walked up the main road to the smaller path leading to the village center.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">She walked up to a handsome wood door with its carved slats and glass windows, which she opened without hesitation, although this was not her house. Entering the common area of the Elders\' house, in this place, required no special authorization. Everyone in the community was free and welcome to enter, as it was understood that all were unified in the goal of the health, happiness, and survival of their community. And this place was where final decisions were usually made.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">Her entry was greeted by a muffled \"hallooo!\" from a connecting room, where old man Silus was apparently occupied. Audrey paced back and forth, thinking about Edward and what they would do after his boat was unloaded. Shortly Silus walked in and warmly acknowledged her; \"What is the news dear?\". She replied \"I saw his boat just now. The trip took longer than usual.\" Silus nodded and reached into the pocket of his shirt, removing a folded piece of paper with some hand-written text on it. He handed it to Audrey who took it smiling, thanked him and departed the way she\'d come in.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">Audrey\'s next stop was on the other side of the village where she would gather some hands to unload the boat. With the dockhands, she returned to the shore where she saw Edward\'s boat and they arrived just as his boat was landing.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">The ritual of trade was as much a part of joy as it was a chore. Edward took Audrey in his arms as the dock workers efficiently stacked the packages and flats of imported goods onto their wagon. After tying the boat securely, they all left toward town, Edward and Audrey\'s hands clasped.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">Such was the vast bulk of their time spent, growing, manufacturing and otherwise preparing goods for trade or use by their own people. The division between \"work\" and \"recreation\" blurred to an extent that the two were almost one. Everyone in the community worked and played as an organism, in symbiosis with neighboring villages and their people. Peace was not always easy, but the trade, they found, was a direct and powerful rebuttal to every conflict.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">It had long been the way of these villages to prefer individual farms, when members were physically able, over centralized commercial-style systems. The \"distributor\" model was tried long ago, and finally abandoned when they learned of its shortcomings. Namely, that such frameworks preclude individuals from trading between communities. Forcing everyone to use the centralized system destroyed inter-village relations by eliminating \"unfair\" or \"unauthorized\" trade. Centralization, it seemed, required measuring of allotments, and bureaucracy. Since those households which traded with outsiders obviously needed more, sometimes vastly more goods than ordinary households, their ability to trade was sacrificed for the convenience of centralization, and so too were myriad trade channels.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">But the Elders understood all this, and every village had a strong, compassionate core of administrators who ensured that the eras of conflict would not return. They did this not only by way of operational prudence but by making education the highest priority. Basing schooling on truth and historical accuracy was, they found, the best way to avoid social failure, and to preserve the health and happiness of their people.&nbsp;</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color: #fff;line-height:1.2em;margin:20px;text-align:justify;font-size:16px\">\n<center>end</center><center><br></center>\n</div>', '2022-09-12 14:43:51', 145, 61, 'whitehot robot', 'other directions - a short story', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600085, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 16px;color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1.1em;\">\n<center>the civic challenge</center><center><br></center>\nA lot is said about \"common courtesy\", \"decency\", and \"social responsibility\", but also about \"liberty\" and respect for \"consent\" in all matters demanding an agreement. The expectation of adherence to a social contract flies in the face of expectations for maximizing consent. How does one reconcile these two, very important aspects of civil society?</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 16px;color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1.1em;\">This ongoing question and answer form the purpose and challenge of all social structure. On one hand, a person is free to abide by the unwritten social agreement or not. But on the other hand must not inflict injury to others regardless of their degree of participation. Those who exercise their right to abstain from affiliation face a very real problem with survival, being codependent on the others, showing that liberty, ironically, depends on some element of Socialism.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 16px;color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1.1em;\">In conclusion, everyone decides their own level of involvement, but those who choose to acknowledge and be involved in their communities are burdened with provision for all members, or else the line between animals and humanity blurs, stability fails, and society collapses. But respect and provision must be the norm, even and especially for those who wish to remain independent.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 16px;color: #fff; margin: 20px;text-align: justify; line-height: 1.1em;\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2022-10-29 14:15:02', 145, 58, 'whitehot robot', 'the civic challenge', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600086, '<div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">\n<center>\"transgressence\"</center><center><br></center>\"Transgressence\" is an anecdotal contraction of transgression and essence, and this text is an exploration of what many people cannot seem to agree on as a concise definition.<br></div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">An effect of any environment in which laws and policies govern behavior, is the prevailing mentality of needing to find The Rule. To observe and remember which literal actions are permitted, and keep at the ready an accusation of hypocrisy when someone else is seen to do something for which one has been punished.</div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">There are many follies here, the biggest of which is that impropriety (wrongdoing), arises not from WHAT is done, but HOW and WHY it is done.</div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">The impetus, motivation, spirit, and ultimate effect of an action defines its propriety (or transgressence), not whether the given thing has been done before to ill effect.</div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">But proving motive, spirit, and even effect is problematic, so we opt instead to unilaterally proscribe random activities as they create problems. It should be absurdly obvious that EVENTUALLY, on a long enough timeline, every possible action will create a serious problem, and if precedent is the primary reason for rules then a predictable narrowing of a pathetic whitelist of permitted activities will eventually take the place of all reason and judgement.</div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">For example, a given statement in another context, even if phrased identically, can mask an opposite desire to be understood, or mean the difference between hate speech and something actually constructive. So to prohibit the statement irrespective of context, is a violent disservice to everyone. The same is true for every law or policy pertaining to actions out of context.</div><div style=\"margin:20px;font-family:courier;font-size:20px;color:#fff;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em\">\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-01-15 02:25:44', 145, 42, 'whitehot robot', '\"transgressence\"', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600087, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">\n<center>need to know</center><center><br></center>Many of us hear eventually that \"knowledge is power\". Then, very few of us are told that some knowledge is a liability. Businesses and authoritarian groups often classify information as proprietary or sensitive, disbursing it as a controlled substance on a \"need to know\" basis. But unilateral rules tend to do more harm than good, especially when it comes to access to information.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">So what becomes the guideline for sensitive information? It is foolish to hide nothing, just as it is foolish to hide everything. There are several clues which inform direction, including truth\'s non-self-contradictory nature, and the effects of knowledge on perception making things appear to multiply or disappear in concert with emphasis or omissions.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">The best practice, if one exists, is a policy of openness without pursuit. However, this is a policy of the receiver not the possessor of knowledge. The subject of deception is relevant to any discussion of access to information. The <b>spirit </b>of communication defines its quality, not the information itself. A desire to be understood must exist in every messenger, and like many things assumed to be volitional (e.g. trust, respect, love, forgiveness, etc.), accurate, helpful communication cannot be forced.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">It\'s ironic that so much energy and time is wasted protecting information that cannot be compartmentalized, when a campaign aimed at educating people as to how and why it is critical to literally \"mind their own business\" would actually solve the problem.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\"><br>\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-01-24 14:28:51', 145, 65, 'whitehot robot', 'need to know', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600088, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">\n<center>the cost of wealth</center><center><br></center>More commonly understood than in the past, money problems affecting all who use it are still mysterious to those who assume incorrectly that everything boils down to a financial problem.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">\nThe true cost of being wealthy is the freedom to disengage, to be at complete peace in any moment, and to reflexively extend any benefit of doubt one wishes. A real example of this is seen in many successful businesspeople, in their recruitment of talent. Some find that their worries are never quite allayed as to whether prospective employees are really not agents of the competition or of past failed opponents.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">As usual, the reasons for being wealthy in the first place are clues as to its propriety. If it is mainly to insulate and defend oneself and his family, it is safe to say the wealth is actually subtracting from his quality of life. But if the wealth is mainly employed proactively toward a (benevolent) enterprise for the purpose of furthering it, the wealth may be a positive element.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">It can be helpful to always bear in mind a \"perfect world\" in which defensive reactions are unnecessary within civilized society. And in such a hypothetical world, absurd power and wealth have no utility. But imagination and hypothetical worlds are something most people are unaccustomed to envisioning.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; text-align: justify; line-height:1.1em;margin:20px;\">\n<center><br></center><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-01-25 13:40:46', 145, 70, 'whitehot robot', 'the cost of wealth', '', 0, 0, ''),
