(600095, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>involuntary positions</center><center><br></center>\nThere are many features to privacy. It encapsulates personal space, defining a boundary within which access is permitted conditionally upon consent. It also enables people to function normally by enabling them to ignore things that should be ignored. Without privacy, everyone is forced into a position in response to those around them.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\">\nConsider an environment in which rules and consequences inform proper behavior. In such an environment, without privacy, an authority is forced into a position to react to everything contrary to the rules. This is inappropriate and embarrassing for both the authority and for those subject to their actions.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\">\nPrivacy is not only critical to a functioning community, but connected, unilateral rules are as unsupportable as a complete absence of privacy. And in an environment with zero privacy AND unilateral rules, a society\'s days are numbered, predictably, in the few.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\">&nbsp;\n\n\n<center>* * *</center><center><br></center>In conclusion, privacy defines the boundary of personal space, without which there is no individuality or anything that depends on it such as free-will, credit, or culpability. <b>Accountability</b>&nbsp;therefore, depends on privacy. Privacy is a gem to be protected by way of responsible choices.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\"><br></div>\n<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.1em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-01-29 23:53:51', 145, 59, 'whitehot robot', 'involuntary positions', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600096, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>empowered managers and disruptions</center><center><br></center>Challenges to conventional correctional/criminal action are often received with skepticism, traditionalists citing concerns for practical enforcement, consistency, and safety when alternatives to hard rules are suggested. In no world can (or should) EVERYONE be expected to be civil, respectful, and nondisruptive, but alternatives to prison and contemporary criminal justice do exist.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Understanding criminal behavior as being some combination of neurological and educational impairment is key to addressing it effectively. The vast majority of criminal/unsupportable behaviors are products of substance abuse and other controllable, temporary factors. As such, the actual need to \"arrest\" people will always remain, but a medical and/or basic needs emphasis represents a factual point of correctional action, versus blind detention and court proceedings.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\"Police\", in a needs-based system resemble care takers more than soldiers but perform the usual task of responding to emergencies and asserting force when needed.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Detention will always be necessary, but to avoid the deleterious effects known to accompany traditional imprisonment, facilities should be designed from the start with the goal of either total rehabilitation, relocation to assisted, permanent housing, or euthanization in extreme cases. Detention should also never be for a purpose other than the expedient, practical handling of individuals. I.e. not as a deterrent or punishment as such is counterproductive, retaliatory, and ultimately ineffective as a means of correction.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Revenge is not a form of justice, but tends to be called for by victims, and enacted by courts. As wrong, tragic, and costly as injuries are, they cannot be fixed with yet more injuries.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><br>\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-01-30 18:54:08', 145, 90, 'whitehot robot', 'empowered managers and disruptions', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600097, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>Art with Substance</center><center><br></center>There are basically two kinds of art. That which arises from trauma, both processed and unprocessed, suffering and hard won experience. Or the other kind of art, clowns and ballerinas, figuratively.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><br>\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-07 17:02:32', 145, 82, 'whitehot robot', 'Art types', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600098, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>the gravity of belief</center><center><br></center>Are you ready? Ready for the biggest thing to hit psychology since Pavlovian Conditioning? Step aside \"confirmation bias\" and make room for \"dependency bias.\"</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Dependency bias is orders of magnitude more influential than other biases, due to its \"gravity\". Consider that people are born with many basic \"starter\" programs, behavioral software coded by millions of years of evolution. Among the most central and powerful of instincts is the inclination toward self-preservation. The survival instinct affects every decision people make, a lens through which information is unconsciously filtered. It is predictably observed that people tend to believe in all the things (and systems) upon which they <u>depend</u> for survival.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Dependency bias appears as the reflex to act first and question second, all instructions from authorities/employers etc. In particular, when one\'s paycheck comes from a given institution or group, there is tremendous \"gravity\" surrounding said group\'s doctrines and mission, regardless of validity. Even if the most objective, actively questioning employee or citizen were to acknowledge a fault, remembering and continuing to object to this fault a day, week or year later, becomes very difficult.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><br>\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-07 18:38:59', 145, 86, 'whitehot robot', 'the gravity of belief', '', 0, 0, '');
INSERT INTO `words` (`id`, `text`, `date`, `userID`, `views`, `author`, `title`, `description`, `private`, `allowDownload`, `tags`) VALUES
(600101, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>the hearts of subjects</center><center><br></center>When a topic or field of study seems dry and uninteresting, this is exactly when it should be reexamined. For many reasons, including misunderstanding, miscommunication, and even intentional deception, certain subjects fail to reveal their hidden gems. But every major subject, of course has gems or would not be a major thing in the first place.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Mathematics, philosophy, politics, and many others are frequently, badly represented by conventional educators. Ask anyone \"what is philosophy?\" for example and they will begin listing off names and specific branches, if you\'re lucky. Or obscure, irrelevant garbage if not. But philosophy existed even before the people with those names lived, and before those branches were recognized. The study of truth and its myriad ways of interconnecting has mystified thinkers since the dawn of language. Philosophy <u>decides</u> which side will win a war, before the war is fought. Philosophy determines who will be successful, and for how long. No? How can it do this? Simply, truth endures, and falsehood erodes. The philosopher learns to recognize truth and leverage it to his or her advantage. So, <u>why</u> philosophy? Because it illuminates the <u>only</u> path forward atop solid foundations.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Mathematics, similarly, and every poorly understood or badly introduced area of knowledge contains invaluable tools. Resources for health and happiness. Pease and prosperity. Practical value, and genuinely interesting substance once properly grasped.<br><center><br></center><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-19 21:17:58', 145, 88, 'whitehot robot', 'the hearts of subjects', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600102, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>faith</center><center><br></center>\"Cultural Inertia\" is the tendency of a behavior, ideology, or social construct to persist throughout time (generations) or geography. In Western Culture, examples of cultural inertia include unquestioning fidelity to capital-driven economic systems, democracy, and, within major religions, advocacy of faith.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">But unquestioned behaviors have no merit until substantiated in contexts. Democracy, it turns out, is unsupportable when the \"will of the people\" is subverted or toxic. Capitalism as well is counterproductive without a genuinely \"free market,\" which competition per se does not automatically ensure. And faith, while vital in desperate times, has utility only when planning has failed.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">The gospel \"wisdom\" handed down from the Bible and countless platitudes is not always best to follow, as should be obvious by its frequent self-contradictions. Indeed, blind faith is observed most strongly in those who question nothing, by definition. Boiling this down: when reality becomes unacceptable, fantasy and belief (or faith) therein, becomes irresistible. In other words, faith is often a form of detachment and a survival reflex for traumatized psyches.<br><br>\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-19 21:25:10', 145, 94, 'whitehot robot', 'faith', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600103, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>modes &amp; roles of ownership</center><center><br></center>A less well-known feature of ownership is emotional investment. To care about someone or something, one must have a stake in it. Conversely, without ownership of a process or thing, motivation to protect it can, at best, only be simulated by proxy via money or other compensation.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\"Modes\" of ownership can be thought to take one of two forms: direct, or vicarious. Direct ownership is the kind everyone understands. But, again less well-known is the latter form, as when direct ownership is revokable, or contingent upon a licensing scheme. The effect of blocking access or possessions is one of usurping some or all of the actual ownership. A.k.a \"vicarious ownership\".</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">A distinct hazard is presented by \"red-light-first\" systems in that <u>everything</u> is partly owned, vicariously, by an authority. This is yet one more reason to prefer the alternative, a figurative \"green light first\" system in which error happens always on the side of (cautious) optimism, vs. cowardice.<br><center><br></center><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-19 21:31:24', 145, 97, 'whitehot robot', 'modes & roles of ownership', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600104, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>careful what you wish for</center><center><br></center>\nConcerning criminal justice, law enforcement, and conventional correctional policies, a prevailing, unwritten expectation upon officers and employees therein is to \"find who dunnit\". On the surface, this may seem an obviously reasonable expectation, but \"who\" can be extremely slippery to scope and define.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\"Who\" involves establishment of identity, which depends on several concrete assumptions: 1) that individual culpability exists to a sufficient degree as to press charges, and 2) that establishing \"who\" proactively is a defensible endeavor. To clarify, \"who\" may involve a database, surveillance, and/or any means necessary to document and identify suspects. This sticky business is complicated further when questions of \"preventative safety\" allow proactive case building (a.k.a. profiling), and amount to a \"red light first\" system in which, eventually all potentially harmful activity must be approved by an authority.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Herein lies the fatal flaw with knowing \"who\" the people are, that edge cases and rarer, corner cases, end up being denied on grounds of caution, precedent, and non-necessity. The eventual outcome of every red-light-first system is a shrinking of the surface of actual liberty with every law passed in REACTION to crimes. Eventually, a narrow whitelist of behavior takes the place of a once verdantly free environment, and dystopia ensues in earnest.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-02-21 18:15:39', 145, 90, 'whitehot robot', 'careful what you wish for', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600105, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center></center>\nline<br>\nline<br>\nline<br>\n<center></center>\n</div>', '2023-02-24 18:13:52', 145, 30, 'whitehot robot', '', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600106, 'edskS886NvjYLaV75AgZU9qhjVacEZHazMoMNWwNtoQZnFEUyAmVax3Q4MWmjpoCgppULqRW2gf4CPxi9ksAcp6yaKvTRQUaVy<br><br><br>\n\npredict dose camp submit solar stool cushion pioneer skill become topple spike', '2023-03-01 18:49:04', 145, 28, 'whitehot robot', 'temple private key', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600107, '035431', '2023-03-04 18:45:00', 145, 27, 'whitehot robot', 'coinbase recover pin', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600108, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>the challenge</center><br>Much is sacrificed upon the altar of necessity. Everyone knows, good intentions aside, the day is defined by what is or is not practical. Routinely we are reminded that \"life is not fair\" and \"ignorance is no excuse,\" but how convenient these sayings make it to dispense with the work of checking facts. And it is work.<br><br>Life truly is not fair, but it is the <u>duty</u> of all who partake of civilization to endeavor to correct this. Ignorance <u>is</u> an excuse, despite urges to cut corners and rush to judgement.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">The perennial challenge is to remain alert to the demand of civilization to render fairness as its chief export. To do this, some obvious conditions are prerequisite. Namely charging <u>individuals</u> for only their own, voluntary, knowing actions. Not the actions of others or a group to which they may belong. As well, the challenge includes separating what someone has done, from what has been done <u>to</u> them. For example, assuming that a victim is less qualified due to that fact alone, would be unsupporatble.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">It is tempting to learn the background of others. To build a model of the person, mentally, by which hypothetical scenarios may be estimated in terms of probability. Have they been \"known\" to act or speak in connected ways? Such biasing data <u>creates</u> a reality, past, present and future, and opposes justice by way of poisoning the objectivity of would-be judges before the facts are in.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-03-09 21:19:41', 145, 72, 'whitehot robot', 'the challenge', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600109, '.demo for(x.fillRect(0,0,i=(w=1e3)*2,i);i--;x.clearRect(w+(i%1e3-w/2)/120/(Z=3+C(p))*w,540+S(p)/Z*w,s=250/Z/Z,s))p=i/80+C(t/2)*12+(i&gt;1e3?3.1:0)', '2023-03-09 23:57:21', 145, 23, 'whitehot robot', '', '', 1, 0, ''),
(600110, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>Gravitation over Astronomical Distances</center><br><img src=\"https://srmcgann.github.io/assets/Bvp8a.gif\" data-high-res-src=\"//srmcgann.github.io/assets/Bvp8a.gif\" class=\"pannable-image\" id=\"asset\" style=\"height: 200px;float:left;margin:20px;\">Observing a haphazard configuration of simulated particles with mass and gravity, galactic structures emerge with an important, notable rate of diminishing over distance: one of a very different rate than other observable properties of space, matter &amp; energy such as the well-known diminishing of light (luminance/d²). That is, with gravity, fall-off occurs at a tremendously higher rate, in the order of (gravity/d²º), and possibly at an increasingly exponential curve with distance.</div><img style=\"display: inline-block;float:right;-webkit-user-select: none;margin: 20px;background-color: hsl(0, 0%, 90%);height:200px;\" src=\"https://srmcgann.github.io/assets/wWDSh.gif\"><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">From this observation it can be posited that remote structures receding (via red/blue-shift measurements) may not be representative of the majority of observable mass in that our \"expanding universe\" may actually be mostly contracting, except for the farthest observable mass, being effectively \"detached\", while nearer mass remains ensnared by more local gravity, and which may eventually collapse. Therefore, to the question of an ending resembling a runaway expansion or a \"big crunch\", the answer is: both! Indeed, the space between galaxies is proof of this effect, that observable space and matter is in a constant state of simultaneous expansion and collapse due to the high rate of gravitational falloff.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\"><br><center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-03-18 17:13:28', 145, 61, 'whitehot robot', 'Gravitation over Astronomical Distances', '', 0, 0, ''),
(600111, '<div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>On Card Tricks</center><br>There are many grifts, sleight of hand illusions, and \"quicker than the eye\" misdirections, often rolled out at parties or to entertain bored children. But some card tricks are less well-intended, forming the basis of important systems and policies.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Among these malicious deceptions, is the \"Nihilist\'s Grift,\" whereby a symbol or text is presented as truth itself. Which of course, sans dialog, opportunity for clarification, or expansion of context, means whatever the messenger likes it to mean. And when accepted as truth (it may be an actual quote or description of events, pruned selectively of key features) the messenger attains full control of the subject\'s belief.</div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">Another powerful grift which has made a frequent appearance throughout history with invariably hellish outcomes, is the \"Impossible Disproof\" grift. This one takes the form of calling upon an intangible, invented concept as if it were a real, substantial thing, then assigning it to a victim, such as a \"witch\" or \"spy\" or \"criminal\" or other such label, which cannot be disproven because the thing isn\'t real to begin with.<br></div><div style=\"font-family: courier; color:#fff;margin:20px;text-align:justify;line-height:1.3em;font-size:20px\">\n<center>end</center>\n</div>', '2023-03-18 17:20:11', 145, 55, 'whitehot robot', 'On Card Tricks', '', 0, 1, ''),
(600113, '<div style=\"text-align: left; margin: 20px;font-family: courier;color:#fff; line-height:1.2em;\">\n✔ Cube guns<br>\n✔ Reverse Sierpenski<br>\n✔ natural fun<br>\n✔ funnel cake<br>\n✔ Billiards<br>\n✔ sluggo<br>\n✔ geospheres fancy [\"crazy shit\"]<br>\n✔ Branching wormholes<br>\n✔ Marble perspective<br>\n✔ perspective warper revisited<br>\nSpacetime mass/speed visualizer<br>\n</div>', '2023-03-23 14:00:33', 145, 22, 'whitehot robot', 'To do', 'Animations ', 1, 0, ''),
(600114, 'The fear is that empowerment of individuals will yield devils of truth, when in reality intellectual prowess more often than not, leads directly to the understanding that deception is self-defeating.', '2023-03-24 14:09:05', 145, 16, 'whitehot robot', '', '', 0, 0, '');
